
Build a clickable, review-only prototype of "Khong", a private messenger whose interface must look and behave like Telegram Web K (web.telegram.org/k) wherever the two share features. Use React 18 + TypeScript in a single-page app. Use plain CSS in one stylesheet with CSS custom properties. Do NOT use Tailwind or any utility-class CSS framework. Do NOT call any network API, do NOT load fonts, icons, images, or scripts from a CDN, and do NOT use localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB, cookies, or service workers. All data is in-memory mock data. There is no real cryptography: simulate it with timers.

=== 0. NAMING RULES (strict) ===
Never use these words in identifiers, CSS class names, test IDs, ARIA labels, or visible text: hidden, secret, secretSpace, hiddenSpace, stealth, covert, cloak, stego, decoy, fake, dummy, cover, coverSpace, plausible, deniable, chaff, garbage, noise, paddingBlob, isReal, isEmpty, isUsed, isActiveSlot, realSlotCount, usedSlots, spaceCount, duress, panic, panicMode, lockdown, blackout, wipePin, password, passcode, pin, secretCode, unlockPassphrase, secondFactor, vault, safe, secretFolder, privateBox, sandbox, hiddenFolder. Use instead: space, code, hush, lock, contact, contactEntry, isOpen, isCollapsed, visible, sample. To remove an element, render it conditionally (do not toggle a class named after a banned word). CSS values such as "overflow: hidden" and "env(safe-area-inset-top)" are allowed. Never show the words "knock", "slot", "index", or "primary space" in the UI, and never show how many spaces exist.

=== 1. FRAME AND REVIEW TOOLBAR ===
Render the app inside a frame, plus a thin review toolbar ABOVE the frame titled "Review controls (not part of the app)". Controls:
- Viewport: "Mobile 390" (frame 390x844, rounded device outline) / "Desktop 1280" (frame 1280x800).
- Theme: "Light" / "Dark" (sets data-theme on the frame; the real app follows the OS setting).
- "Simulate offline" toggle (shows offline states).
- "Simulate leaving the app" button (triggers lock exactly like Lock now).
- "Reset to first run" button (goes to the Welcome screen with no account).
- "Deliver sample message" button (adds an incoming message to the first chat of the open space, as if an inbox check just ran).
- A note showing the sample codes: Space A code "blue river morning", Space B code "green hill evening" (codes need at least 6 characters). Any other code fails.

