=== 3. LAYOUT ===
Mobile (<768px): stacked navigation. Chat list is the root; chat, contacts, settings and sub-pages push in from the right with a back arrow; sheets rise from the bottom.
Desktop (>=1024px): left column 420px (chat list, search, contacts, settings and their sub-pages slide inside it) + right pane (open chat, or wallpaper with a centered service pill "Select a chat to start messaging"). Contact info opens as a third 420px column at >=1280px, otherwise as an overlay on the right pane.

=== 4. MOCK DATA (obviously sample only) ===
uin(prefix, suffix) = prefix padded with zeros to 60 chars + 4-char suffix, all lowercase hex, 64 chars total. Display UINs in groups of 4; short form = first two groups + " … " + last group (e.g. "a11c e000 … 0001").
This account UIN: uin("c0ffee00","0000").
sampleSpaceA: contacts (newest first):
 1. uin("a11ce000","0001"), key code "AAAA BBBB CCCC DDDD EEEE FFFF GGGG HHHH", name "Sample contact 1"; messages today: in "Sample message: are we still on for six?" 09:12; out "Sample reply: six works." 09:14 sent; in "Sample photo" with a generated gradient image and caption "Sample photo caption" 09:20; out "Sample message waiting for the other side" 09:31 not sent.
 2. uin("b0b00000","0002"), key "BBBB CCCC DDDD EEEE FFFF GGGG HHHH JJJJ", name "Sample contact 2"; yesterday: in "Sample file attached" with file card "sample-report.pdf · 240 KB" 18:02; out "Thanks, sample received." 18:05 sent. Unread badge 1.
 3. uin("ca7ca700","0003"), key "CCCC DDDD EEEE FFFF GGGG HHHH JJJJ KKKK", no name (shows the short UIN); no messages yet.
 Plus one unknown sender chat: title "Unknown sender", key code "DDDD EEEE FFFF GGGG HHHH JJJJ KKKK MMMM", message "Sample message from someone not in your contacts." 08:40.
sampleSpaceB: contacts: 1. uin("d00d0000","0004"), key "EEEE FFFF GGGG HHHH JJJJ KKKK MMMM NNNN", name "Sample contact 4"; one message in "Sample message in another space." 07:55. No unknown senders.
Both spaces show the same Settings rows, menus, and footnotes. Never label either space by name or number on screen.

=== 5. GLOBAL BEHAVIOR ===
- LOCK: "Lock now" (header lock icon, hamburger menu, Privacy and Security), the review button "Simulate leaving the app", and 120 s without pointer or key activity all lock. Lock instantly replaces the whole app with the Lock screen, sets document.title to "Khong", closes every dialog, menu, sheet and toast, and discards drafts, search text, selection, and every message from the screen (contacts, names, and history remain because they are stored encrypted with the space). After the same code opens the space again, show a 2 px indeterminate bar under the chat-list header for 1 s, then the same chats and messages come back.
- KNOCK WAIT: submitting a code on the Lock screen, in the wordmark code sheet (S-08a), or on "Spaces to keep" (S-22), or pressing Enter in Search, ALWAYS waits exactly 2000 ms with the same spinner, then: matching code -> open that space; otherwise -> failure. Never finish early.
- OFFLINE (review toggle): chat list shows a banner under the header with cloud_off "Waiting for network…"; chat header subtitle becomes "Waiting for network…"; new outgoing messages stay in the clock state. Lock screen and knock are unaffected.
- No "Updating…" indicator, no countdown to the next check, no pull-to-refresh.
- Outgoing message states: sending (schedule icon, 800 ms) -> sent (single done check). Never show a double check. A not-sent message shows a red error icon and, under the bubble, small text "Not sent. Khong will try again while this space is open."; tapping it opens a menu "Try again now" / "Delete".
- Unread badges only for chats in the open space. No count in the tab title.
- Links in messages are underlined plain text; tapping shows a dialog "Open this link in your browser?" with "Cancel" / "Open" (Open does nothing in the prototype). No link previews.
- Desktop keys: Enter sends, Shift+Enter newline, Esc closes the top layer, Ctrl/Cmd+F focuses search.

